Fix for "cube appears in front of the panel": `PointerOut` auto-propagates from a row to
all ancestors, but `unhover_row` writes the transparent band colour into whatever entity
it receives. That includes the panel root, whose BackgroundColor feeds
`feathers_in_3d::world3d::sync_mirror` -> `UNodeMaterial3d.color`; alpha 0 discards the
SDF body (border still draws), so the opaque cube behind becomes visible.

This patch is illustrative (line numbers may drift while rig-feathers is edited).
Verified on a copy in `occlusion_probe/rig_dbg` (see `render/probe/fix_tour/`).

--- a/rig-feathers/src/main.rs
+++ b/rig-feathers/src/main.rs
@@ -318,6 +318,7 @@
 fn unhover_row(
     out: On<bevy::picking::events::PointerOut>,
+    rows: Query<&RowText>,
     mut backgrounds: Query<&mut BackgroundColor>,
     selected: Res<Selected>,
 ) {
     let entity = out.entity;
-    if selected.0.contains(&entity) {
+    // `PointerOut` bubbles to every ancestor; only a real row may lose its band.
+    if !rows.contains(entity) || selected.0.contains(&entity) {
         return;
     }
     if let Ok(mut bg) = backgrounds.get_mut(entity) {
         bg.0 = Color::srgba(0.10, 0.14, 0.22, 0.0);
     }
 }
